WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.439
- Hello everyone, I'm Ed McMahon and now--

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:05.000
- Here's Johnny.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.420
- It's time for a clash of the kings,

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.390
or King as the case may be.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.860
IT Chapter Two is heading
into theaters soon

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.210
and to honor everyone's
favorite googly-eyed clown,

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.830
we decided to celebrate his
creator, Mr. Stephen King.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.710
On this show, celebrations
get competitive,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.220
so we're pitting King's
best theatrically-released

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.360
horror film adaptations against each other

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.830
in a winner take all bracket style brawl.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.797
Get your popcorn ready Georgie, pop, pop.

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:30.797
- Pop.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.047
(laughing)

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.430
- Here's how it works.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.600
We took the 16 highest-rated

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.020
Stephen King horror
movies on the tomatometer

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.360
and seeded them accordingly.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.440
So, if you're a fan of Stephen
King's more cult classics

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.910
like a Dreamcatcher, a
Children of the Corn,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.940
sorry, they're not showing up anywhere.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.740
Kids, go out in the field and play.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.050
From this bracket of 16,

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.220
we'll whittle it down
to eight and then four

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.090
and then two and finally we'll crown

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.690
the all time greatest
Steven King scary flick.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.990
Friendly reminder,
although being in prison

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.090
or bullied by Kiefer Sutherland is scary,

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.120
King's drama adaptations
are not a part of this list.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.490
So no Shawshank, no Stand By Me,

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.050
no environmentally conscious mile.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.040
And if you're wondering,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.260
was the original IT released in theaters,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.794
I will simply answer with a polite no.

00:01:18.794 --> 00:01:20.320
- Exactly.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.100
- But, shout out to the OG Pennywise

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.550
who was played by the
legend, Mr. Tim Curry.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.190
One plus one plus two plus one.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.180
- Even if you are right,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.447
that would be one plus
one plus two plus one,

00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:30.480
not one plus two plus one plus one.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.480
- The jump ball's in the air

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.500
and it's time for the sweet 16.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.670
Let's run through these match-ups

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.160
and find out who's
advancing to the next round.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.120
The top-seeded Carrie is going up

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.100
against the 16 seed, Silver Bullet.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.550
Carrie was Stephen King's
first horror novel,

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.560
the one that did well enough
for him to quit teaching.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.400
And the film was his first
big-screen adaptation.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.410
This is why we have all those
other movies to talk about.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.170
Thank you, C Money.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.307
- No I just don't like ruffles--

00:01:55.307 --> 00:01:56.140
- You don't like ruffles?

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.160
You don't have to get ruffles!

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.473
- Silver Bullet, on the other hand...

00:01:58.473 --> 00:01:59.850
Remember that one?

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.510
Mysterious deaths start
happening in a sleepy town

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.450
so Corey Haim and his uncle
have to stop a werewolf.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:06.650
Who plays his uncle?

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.210
Who else but Gary Busey.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.043
- Ta-da!

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.830
- And, despite my affinity
for all things Busey

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.350
and my love of Coors Light,

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.680
Silver Bullet is being stopped

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.760
by the Kevlar known as Carrie.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.940
Carrie advances.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.880
- That's bullshit luck.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:22.840
Bullshit luck!

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.640
- Next up we have
Creepshow versus Christine.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.010
Creepshow was King's screenwriting debut

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.600
and directed by the horror
master himself, George Romero.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.200
It played then and now as
a horror-comedy anthology

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.720
with an eclectic cast that
includes Hal Holbrook,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.630
Ted Danson and Leslie Nielson.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.657
I love it!

00:02:40.657 --> 00:02:43.960
- Cringe and weird Kids.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.730
- However, I would have
to say that Christine

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.040
is the better known property,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.480
simply based on the fact that Christine

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.230
is a car that gets picked on

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.030
and develops a revenge-hungry
mind of its own.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.840
In short, this movie can scare anyone

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.730
who's ever driven a car.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.450
Any Plymouth owners out there? (pop)

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.470
Shout out to you.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.303
Buckle up.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.183
(tires screech)

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.850
The next battle is between
two more recent King movies,

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:10.230
IT from 2017 versus
Pet Sematary from 2019.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:13.120
Both are reimaginings from
their original adaptations,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.580
and while Pet Sematary
did have solid reviews,

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.890
IT was a world-wide phenomenon,

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.330
dominating the box office

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.860
and canceling clown
birthday party performances

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.270
at a record pace.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.951
Pennywise gets the win.

00:03:24.951 --> 00:03:25.784
(clown snarls)

00:03:25.784 --> 00:03:26.617
(children scream)

00:03:26.617 --> 00:03:29.090
We move on to The Shining
versus The Dark Half,

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.130
and to be clear, this is
The Shining from 1979,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.950
not the TV movie starring
Steven Weber from Wings.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.330
Underrated sitcom.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.923
- You burned Helen's house to the ground.

00:03:38.923 --> 00:03:40.300
(laughs)

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.430
- Oops. (chuckles)

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.940
- Speaking of underrated,
The Dark Half has a premise

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:47.560
some might say spawn from
Stephen King's own writer fears.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.210
Timothy Hutton plays an author

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.990
whose pseudonym starts
actually killing people.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.000
- Sorry, Rhett, it's a cutthroat business.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.900
- And while we're on
the subject of authors,

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.160
how about that Jack Torrence?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.550
Dedicated family man and
boy, does he work hard.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.760
The Shining is the all-time classic

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.210
that inspired generations of horror lovers

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.781
and that's why The
Shining is gonna move on.

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:12.281
(piano music)

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.950
Speaking of hotels, our next
fracas is 1408 versus Cujo.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:22.280
Now, Cujo is definitely the
more well-known property

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.270
and has a permanent place
in our cultural zeitgeist.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.010
However, as the stepfather of a dog,

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:29.860
I don't want to perpetuate any media that

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.930
portrays dogs as anything
less than the angels they are.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.960
1408 may be the lesser-known horror film

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.230
that features a hotel,

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.580
but the paranoia of
John Cusack's character

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.660
has a slow burn that doesn't let up.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.185
1408 gets to stay another night.

00:04:43.185 --> 00:04:44.770
- (whispers) You gotta be kidding me.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.400
- The Dead Zone versus 1989's
Pet Sematary is up next.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.650
And remember how I just defended dogs?

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.560
Yeah, I don't feel the
same way about cats,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.460
especially if they're dead already.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.090
I'm totally cool with
cats creeping up the joint

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.570
and the original Pet Sematary

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.890
had a massive effect
on me as an 8-year-old.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:01.723
Why?

00:05:01.723 --> 00:05:03.260
Because my aunt took me to see it

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.640
in the theater when I was but eight.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.820
I don't know why she did it.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.420
It still haunts me to this day.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.030
Sorry, Chris Walken, Pet
Sematary gets to move on.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.220
Man, we just can't escape pets.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.740
Cat's Eye is taking on The Mist

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.420
and the former is another
anthology from King's mind

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.160
and directed, once
again, by George Romero.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.050
Three stories all
featuring the same feline

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.510
running around, making
things uncomfortable,

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.820
and judging the humans.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.641
Just like kitties do in real life.

00:05:30.641 --> 00:05:31.474
(cat meows)

00:05:31.474 --> 00:05:32.790
Meanwhile, The Mist is so creepy

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.660
and dripping with societal metaphors

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.120
that it deserves to advance.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.600
You stick with that flick long enough

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.370
and the payoff features monsters

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.183
and it gets very, very depressing.

00:05:42.218 --> 00:05:44.220
(man yells)

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.440
The Mist advances and any cat that was

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.700
watching this vid, has now turned it off.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.500
Thanks for the click, Garfield.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.340
Our last match up in this round features

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.910
Misery versus the 2013 remake of Carrie.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.220
This was a good remake of Carrie

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.570
and it had plenty of blood,

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.770
but how in the world
would I let Misery lose

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.880
to a cockadoody remake?

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.450
Paul Sheldon finished his book,

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.900
he threw a snowball strike

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.570
and was on top of the world

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.990
until he wound up in a super fan's bed.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:10.823
Eh.

00:06:10.823 --> 00:06:13.770
Misery will have plenty of
company because it gets the win

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.840
and is moving on to the elite eight.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.370
- He didn't get out of the cockadoody car!

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.420
- [Host] And now time for the elite eight.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.120
Our first match up is
Carrie versus Christine.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.210
A car that kills people is a fun idea

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.520
and gives all of us
Herbie the Love Bug fans

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:30.600
something to think about,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.860
but Carrie has transcended
the horror genre

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.860
and become an iconic representation

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.850
of how scary being a teenager can be,

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.140
especially in that family.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:41.480
It's more relatable and thus
infinitely more terrifying.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.690
Plus, I'd hate to think that

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.640
all that pig's blood went to waste.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.738
Carrie advances to the final four.

00:06:46.738 --> 00:06:48.980
(kids laugh)

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.210
- The next match up will
cause a lot of comments.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.043
How do I know this?

00:06:52.043 --> 00:06:53.540
Am I Dionne Warwick?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:57.050
No, but these two flicks
are all-time scary hits.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.020
IT versus The Shining.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:06:59.860
Wow!

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.160
IT was an international
money making juggernaut

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.650
that rebooted at the right time,

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.820
capitalizing on our
love of Stranger Things

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.330
and our fear of clowns.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.680
It made $329 million domestically,

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.820
which more than doubles
The Shining's total.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.868
Yes, I adjusted for inflation.

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:16.150
- Time to float.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.950
- For a clown that only shows up once,

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.240
what, every 27 years, which makes it

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.740
all the more curious that
I'm picking The Shining.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.190
- I'm not real enough for you?

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.230
- I know, I know.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.540
Sometimes it just comes down
to which flick is scarier.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:30.420
The Shining has more all-time horrific

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.700
images that stay with you.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.760
The twins, the big wheel, the elevator,

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.320
the bartender, the bathtub.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.600
Get out of the tub, lady!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.960
You're starting to prune.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.993
And plus, ugh, poor Shelley Duvall.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:43.850
- Yeah.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.810
- Both movies are hits,

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.700
both have sequels coming
out later this year,

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.408
but The Shining is
advancing to the next round.

00:07:49.408 --> 00:07:52.180
(ice clinks against glass)

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.260
Next up is 1408 versus Pet Sematary.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:56.830
This one is an easy call for me,

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.597
but let's tout 1408's
impressive stats first.

00:07:59.597 --> 00:08:03.210
$237 million total at the box office

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.930
and it's 79% fresh on the tomato meter.

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:09.050
Meanwhile, Pet Sematary
made $167.4 million

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.740
at the box office and is
just below fresh at 52%.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.160
However, 1408 is a creepy, psychological

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.970
horror exploration that we saw and went,

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.150
yeah okay it's pretty good.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.210
Pet Sematary is everywhere.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.250
We all know what it is, we're
born with that knowledge.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.708
There's a place that you
do not bury anything.

00:08:25.708 --> 00:08:27.565
(imitating Fred Gwynne)
Sometimes, dead is better.

00:08:27.565 --> 00:08:30.200
- Sometimes, dead is better.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.080
- Also, spoiler alert, no
one dies on screen in 1408.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.010
It's just a wacky night in a hotel room.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.710
Meanwhile, Pet Sematary has this.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:39.753
- Never get out of bed again!

00:08:39.753 --> 00:08:42.053
Never get out of bed again!

00:08:42.053 --> 00:08:43.801
- I was only eight years old!

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:45.260
Eight!

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.010
Pet Sematary's going to the final four.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.500
- I brought you something, mommy.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.920
- Our last movie date match up

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.150
features The Mist versus Misery.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.070
Yeah, I like The Mist

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.640
and it gets credit for being fresh at 72%

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.370
and having some impressive
monster-related deaths.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.450
34 people eat it in this flick.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.650
34!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.210
Well done, fog spiders.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.470
Problem is, The Mist is
running into a buzzsaw

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.590
and her name, Annie Wilkes.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.430
- Oh, I hope I didn't wake you.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.836
- Misery is certified fresh at 90%,

00:09:13.836 --> 00:09:16.930
considered an all time
classic, won Academy Awards,

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:19.440
and even though it only
has two deaths in it,

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.754
we also see feet getting clubbed.

00:09:21.754 --> 00:09:22.587
Eww.

00:09:22.587 --> 00:09:23.720
Between that and Zelda,

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.780
I am limping out of this studio today.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.600
Misery gets the win.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.800
- The operation was called hobbling.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.850
- You are looking live at the final four.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.840
So the film that started it all, Carrie,

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.580
now faces its most daunting challenge yet,

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.290
The Overlook Hotel.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:41.250
Most of us were a little
scared of prom anyway,

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.660
so Carrie had a leg up.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.750
But as someone that
stays in a lot of hotels,

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.720
The Shining gets in your
head and never leaves.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.900
Why does any hotel still have room 237?

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.170
Y'all don't have a 13th floor

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.670
but you're cool with the dead
zombie lady in the bathtub?

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.470
Get your priorities straight, hotels!

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:59.130
Signed, a Loyal Bonvoy Member.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.700
Anyway, all due credit to the pair

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.280
of Academy Award nominated
performances in Carrie

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.160
from Sissy Spacek and Piper Laurie,

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.030
but The Shining holds
up as the scarier flick.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.740
This is despite the fact that The Shining

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.870
not only earned zero Oscar nominations,

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.580
Shelley Duvall and Stanley Kubrick

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.130
each received a Razzy nomination.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.780
Not appreciated in its own
time, or by the author,

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.850
but I'm here to give The Shining its due.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.160
All work and no play makes Jack a dull boy

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.964
but Jack's movie is playing in the finals.

00:10:27.964 --> 00:10:31.000
(man sings creepily)

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.650
And in the other final four matchup,

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.880
it's a real underdog story.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.590
But you don't want to
play with these dogs.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:37.440
Or these cats.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.840
Or anything else buried in Pet Sematary.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.780
- It's misspelled, but
that's what it says.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.730
- This film is such a cool concept

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.950
and features some truly chilling moments,

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.920
both from events central to the plot--

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.930
- Don't let him go in the road, son!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.180
- And from random back stories

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.100
put in just to give me nightmares.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.170
I'm going to twist your spine.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:58.060
(laughs evilly)

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:00.263
But Misery has two A-list actors

00:11:00.263 --> 00:11:02.330
giving tremendous performances,

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:05.290
including the Oscar-winning
turn for Kathy Bates.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.310
We cannot overstate how important

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.930
that win was for horror movies,

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.400
second only to comedies,
in terms of film genres

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.190
that simply don't get enough
credit come awards season.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.570
Just ask Toni Colette, who I'm still upset

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.340
wasn't nominated for Hereditary.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.110
The film builds suspense so well,

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.910
has some viscerally terrifying moments

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.583
and gave us a villain for all times.

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.250
- I don't want her spirit.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.210
- If there's a Mount
Rushmore for movie villains,

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.400
it's gotta be the Wicked
Witch of the West,

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:34.286
Darth Vader, Annie Wilkes
and Chet from Weird Science.

00:11:34.286 --> 00:11:36.580
- You're stewed, buttwad.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:41.018
- Misery buries Pet Sematary
and moves on the the finals.

00:11:41.018 --> 00:11:42.543
- I'm my number one fan.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:49.730
- And now, we've arrived
at the championship game.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.540
Steven King's all-time
theatrically-released

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.390
horror film adaptations,

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:57.690
it all comes down to
Misery versus The Shining.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.850
In this corner, we have a crazed author

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.730
and his opponent is someone

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.410
who would probably love his books.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.850
Jack versus Annie.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:08.428
Snow versus, well, more snow.

00:12:08.428 --> 00:12:10.630
(wind howls)

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.730
To determine my ultimate
Stephen King movie,

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:15.390
I'm looking beyond all
the box office accolades

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:17.440
and performances that
got these flicks here.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.870
To earn the crown, I'm looking
into their all-time legacy.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.270
Where do these films rank

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.920
in the pantheon of
all-mighty horror cinema?

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.630
Misery was perhaps King's
most prized possession,

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.900
or at least the one he was
most strict about optioning.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.500
He only wanted Rob Reiner to make the film

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.360
and that was only after Reiner
did such a fantastic job

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:37.580
with another King story, Stand by Me.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.067
Speaking of Rob Reiner,

00:12:39.067 --> 00:12:40.910
Misery's success was a reaffirmation

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.140
that you didn't have to be
considered a horror director

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.840
to make a great scary flick.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.330
Reiner was coming off rom-com
hits like When Harry Met Sally

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.530
and The Princess Bride
when he made Misery,

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.370
but if you wanna talk
about big-time directors

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.100
venturing into the world of
horror, enter Stanley Kubrick.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.570
Despite the protests from King himself,

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.810
The Shining has become
a cultural touchstone

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:03.000
that resonates with
generations of movie lovers.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.400
For example, how about
the extended sequence

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.760
in 2017's Ready Player One

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.380
that takes place in The Overlook Hotel.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:13.680
It's just another reminder of
how truly scary The Shining is

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.020
and how horrifying hotels
can be at 3:00 a.m.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.170
If you see a bartender in
the middle of the might,

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.710
in a hotel, it is a ghost.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:21.760
Go back to your room.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.420
- It is slow tonight, isn't it?

00:13:26.617 --> 00:13:28.650
(laughs maniacally)

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:31.070
- Misery is an undisputed
classic scary movie.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.970
It features unforgettable performances,

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.570
spine-tingling suspense
wrought by Rob Reiner,

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.040
and the film can claim
what few horror movies can,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.150
Academy Awards.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.200
Meanwhile, The Shining
has found its own place

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.710
in the pop culture lexicon,

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.910
and that legacy only
seems to grow stronger

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.290
with each passing year.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:49.320
To be one of the top films
of both Stanley Kubrick

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:53.190
and Jack Nicholson's legendary
careers is no small feat.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.960
And now, to declare my winner.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.450
Quick sidebar to heighten the tension.

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:58.060
Barnes and Noble did a cool article

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.660
that ragged the King horror movies

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.160
in terms of faithfulness
to their source material.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.100
Misery was the most faithful

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:06.220
and The Shining was number 13,

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.540
which makes it all the more nutty

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.284
that I'm proclaiming The
Shining as my winner!

00:14:10.284 --> 00:14:11.320
(claps)

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.500
It's the scariest one to me.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.840
I know not to go driving

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.630
during a blizzard on mountainous terrain

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.130
but to not stay at hotels?

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:20.100
Come on, I'm a comedian,
that's unavoidable.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:22.030
Tickets at MarkEllisLive.com

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.350
The Shining takes the prize

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.960
and just like they do for March Madness,

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.716
cue the song One Shining Moment.

00:14:27.716 --> 00:14:31.216
♪ You reached down inside ♪

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.073
- Anything you say, Lloyd.

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:36.700
Anything you say.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.580
- The good news is, I'm
not gonna sing anymore.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:39.650
The really good news,

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.740
is that all of this is just my opinion.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.880
Stephen King certainly
doesn't agree with me.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:44.900
How about you?

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.810
Now it is your turn to
vote for the all-time best

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:50.170
Stephen King horror film adaptation.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.660
We'll post our bracket below.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.090
All you have to do is leave a
comment below with your take.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:54.923
What's the best?

00:14:54.923 --> 00:14:55.920
What's the scariest?

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.220
Which movie do you wish
was in the Sweet 16?

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.430
Any Sleepwalker fans out there?

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.340
Salem's Lot?

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:02.500
Let us know right now.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.680
Thanks for tuning in and remember kids,

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:08.180
if a jittery old lady made
you cookies then got naked,

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.870
she's probably a murderous clown.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:10.913
Have a great day.

00:15:10.913 --> 00:15:13.496
(upbeat music)

